WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.420 --> 00:00:05.070
The Penguin features prominently in Matt Reeves's
"The Batman," but did you know that this famous

00:00:05.070 --> 00:00:09.280
comics character has seen many different versions
portrayed over the years?

00:00:09.280 --> 00:00:13.330
Stay tuned to get a look at how the Penguin
from "The Batman" should really look.

00:00:13.330 --> 00:00:15.250
Warning: Spoilers ahead.

00:00:15.250 --> 00:00:20.080
Batman has been adapted for the big screen
by numerous filmmakers, all of whom have interpreted

00:00:20.080 --> 00:00:22.770
the character and his stories in unique ways.

00:00:22.770 --> 00:00:27.550
Tim Burton embraced the pulpier element of
Gotham's caped crusader while adding his trademark

00:00:27.550 --> 00:00:33.329
gothic-horror stylings to the proceedings
in 1989's "Batman" and its sequel, "Batman

00:00:33.329 --> 00:00:34.329
Returns."

00:00:34.329 --> 00:00:38.190
Joel Schumacher, meanwhile, leaned into the
campier side of the Dark Knight when he was

00:00:38.190 --> 00:00:41.539
tasked with helming "Batman Forever" and "Batman
&amp; Robin."

00:00:41.539 --> 00:00:46.309
Elsewhere, Christopher Nolan opted for a more
grounded and realistic approach to crime-fighting

00:00:46.309 --> 00:00:48.000
in the "Dark Knight" trilogy.

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:52.030
The latest iteration of the World's Greatest
Detective on screen comes from filmmaker Matt

00:00:52.030 --> 00:00:57.329
Reeves, best known for his work on "Cloverfield"
and the most recent "Planet of the Apes" trilogy.

00:00:57.329 --> 00:01:02.269
"The Batman" is a neo-noir thriller with horror
elements, boasting a story that focuses on

00:01:02.269 --> 00:01:07.340
a psychologically damaged Bruce Wayne and
his alter-ego Batman, as he proclaims himself

00:01:07.340 --> 00:01:08.780
to be vengeance incarnate.

00:01:08.780 --> 00:01:09.880
"I'm Vengeance."

00:01:09.880 --> 00:01:15.170
Naturally, "The Batman" also takes some creative
liberties with the source material and presents

00:01:15.170 --> 00:01:18.290
familiar characters in fresh and interesting
ways.

00:01:18.290 --> 00:01:23.289
The film's depiction of the Penguin, for instance,
is a huge departure from any other incarnations

00:01:23.289 --> 00:01:24.740
of the villain on the screen.

00:01:24.740 --> 00:01:27.439
But how is the character supposed to look?

00:01:27.439 --> 00:01:31.869
The Penguin, otherwise known as Oswald Cobblepot,
has been one of the most popular villains

00:01:31.869 --> 00:01:34.009
in the "Batman" canon for decades.

00:01:34.009 --> 00:01:39.499
Known for his umbrellas, cigars, extravagant
tuxedo, and trademark waddle, the crime kingpin

00:01:39.499 --> 00:01:42.240
has a recognizable look that just screams
villainy.

00:01:42.240 --> 00:01:47.499
Over the years, he has been portrayed by the
likes of Burgess Meredith, Danny DeVito, and

00:01:47.499 --> 00:01:52.149
Robin Lord Taylor, all of whom established
a firm image of the character in the pop-culture

00:01:52.149 --> 00:01:53.149
imagination.

00:01:53.149 --> 00:01:57.439
However, Colin Farrell's Penguin in "The Batman"
isn't the same menace who's graced previous

00:01:57.439 --> 00:01:59.000
movies and TV shows.

00:01:59.000 --> 00:02:04.130
For a start, the cigar, top hat, and tuxedo
are all gone in exchange for everyday gangster

00:02:04.130 --> 00:02:05.130
clothing.

00:02:05.130 --> 00:02:09.149
He does carry an umbrella at times, but it
doesn't possess the ability to fire bullets.

00:02:09.149 --> 00:02:14.709
Farrell, who lobbied for a cigar, discussed
the changes in a December 2021 interview with

00:02:14.709 --> 00:02:15.709
Empire.

00:02:15.709 --> 00:02:19.790
The actor acknowledged the key alterations
made to the character, but he also wants fans

00:02:19.790 --> 00:02:23.540
to know that it's still early in Cobblepot's
quest to become the familiar foe.

00:02:23.540 --> 00:02:24.540
He revealed:

00:02:24.540 --> 00:02:28.750
"Oz is not yet fully inhabiting the mythology
of the Penguin and doesn't take too kindly

00:02:28.750 --> 00:02:30.269
to the [Penguin] moniker."

00:02:30.269 --> 00:02:34.430
It remains to be seen how the Penguin will
evolve in the "Batman" franchise moving forward.

00:02:34.430 --> 00:02:37.480
However, he will return to the fold in a substantial
way.

00:02:37.480 --> 00:02:42.620
Warner Bros. has major plans for the character,
so fans can look forward to a more fleshed-out

00:02:42.620 --> 00:02:44.409
story at a later date.

00:02:44.409 --> 00:02:47.939
While he probably should have died in "The
Batman," the Penguin survived the chaos and

00:02:47.939 --> 00:02:51.049
will live to fight another day in Gotham's
criminal underbelly.

00:02:51.049 --> 00:02:56.159
Warner Bros. has ambitious plans for the character,
who is set to receive his own spin-off TV

00:02:56.159 --> 00:02:57.159
series.

00:02:57.159 --> 00:03:01.470
The story will reportedly chronicle Cobblepot's
rise from mid-level Gotham gangster into the

00:03:01.470 --> 00:03:07.050
grandiose crime kingpin he's typically depicted
as in the movies, TV shows, and comics.

00:03:07.050 --> 00:03:11.350
Details about the series are being kept close
to the vest right now, but early reports have

00:03:11.350 --> 00:03:16.439
compared it to "Scarface," a mob saga that
follows one gangster's ascension in the criminal

00:03:16.439 --> 00:03:17.439
underworld.

00:03:17.439 --> 00:03:19.349
"Say hello to my little friend."

00:03:19.349 --> 00:03:23.099
Of course, it's highly likely that some changes
will be made to the Penguin character in this

00:03:23.099 --> 00:03:25.620
version of the DC franchise.

00:03:25.620 --> 00:03:28.969
Most characters differ from their older counterparts
in some way, after all.

00:03:28.969 --> 00:03:33.060
"The Batman" gives us a menacing serial killer
version of the Riddler, who wouldn't seem

00:03:33.060 --> 00:03:34.709
out of place in a movie like "Se7en."

00:03:34.709 --> 00:03:39.329
Then there's the Joker, who, despite being
hidden behind a cell door during his brief

00:03:39.329 --> 00:03:44.250
cameo in the movie, doesn't appear to resemble
any previous versions of the character.

00:03:44.250 --> 00:03:48.269
In short, it remains to be seen if the Penguin
will rock top hats and fire bullets from an

00:03:48.269 --> 00:03:50.860
umbrella in the spin-off series and future
movies.

00:03:50.860 --> 00:03:56.000
At the same time, the unpredictability is
exciting in its own right, and it'll be interesting

00:03:56.000 --> 00:03:58.260
to see it all unfold.

